  "review": {
    "review": "The hero was alive when the planner stopped. Decision 2879 (log line 8153) explored at 49/55 HP despite a remembered upgrade behind magical fire, an untested potion, and an unused 24-turn healing allowance. The regular recovery target was only 65%, while guarded frost testing required 95% (tools/mage_policy.py:755; tools/puzzle_supplies.py:879). Earlier identification revealed levitation, not frost. The strength potion was later collected and used; the upgrade remained blocked. Decision 3147 ended with 43/60 HP and mandatory-preparation-unresolved, not a death. The proposal aligns bounded recovery with that preparation prerequisite; it preserves the wait allowance, hazard checks, identification rules and mandatory pickup. A reduced public-evidence fixture fails two assertions on original policy and passes on the candidate; the full suite passes 2,212 tests with four skips. This establishes recovery selection, not sufficient healing, potion identity, puzzle completion or prevention of the terminal failure. The truncated played-source comparison supports no additional behavioral improvement claim.",
    "learnings": "Budget health for required potion preparation before exploring away from an unfinished upgrade room. Recovery should recognize the existing test threshold without extending waits or lowering safety requirements. Keep unknown potion identities unknown and require actual extinguishing and pickup receipts."
  },
